Description: Implements algorithms for terrestrial, mobile, and airborne lidar processing, tree detection,
      segmentation, and attribute estimation (Donager et al., 2021) <doi:10.3390/rs13122297>, and hierarchical
      habitat patch delineation using 'PatchMorph' (Girvetz & Greco, 2007) <doi:10.1007/s10980-007-9104-8>.
      Version 2.0 introduces an explicit staged TLS/MLS workflow: find_trees() -> tree_points() -> stem_points()
      -> stem_segments() -> tree_inventory(). Each stage accepts interchangeable method objects, including
      use_raster_eigen(), use_hough(), assign_voronoi(), assign_crop(), assign_graph(), stem_eigen(),
      stem_hough(), seg_ransac_cylinder(), seg_irls_cylinder(), and seg_bf_cylinder(), so detection,
      assignment, classification, and stem-fitting strategies can be swapped without changing the surrounding
      workflow. Additional tools estimate leaf area index, leaf area density, plant area density, canopy
      transmittance, branch and leaf-wood classes, stem volume, tree quality, and targeted stem refits.
      Airborne lidar individual-tree segmentation is supported through 'lidR'-compatible allometric geodesic,
      random-walker, and supervoxel algorithms. Compiled C++ back ends provide Hough stem detection,
      fast nearest-tree assignment, batch cylinder fitting, voxel PAD calculations, and point-cloud geometry
      metrics. Earlier functions such as get_raster_eigen_treelocs(), segment_graph(), classify_stem_points(),
      and segment_stem() remain available for backward compatibility. Built on 'lidR'
      (Roussel et al., 2020) <doi:10.1016/j.rse.2020.112061>.
